{
  "title": "Burn down private helper re-exports from pilot.py",
  "description": "`puppeteer/pilot.py` has become a public façade for private helpers that actually live in `pilot_bridge`, `pilot_game_state`, `pilot_recovery`, `pilot_rendering`, and `pilot_state`. Its `__all__` includes many underscore-prefixed names, and tests assert that those imports are aliases of the implementation modules.\n\
\n\
Retire that façade. Move external callers and tests to the owning modules, and only keep deliberate public symbols on the `pilot` surface. This issue is about the outward API shape, not the deeper internal dependency graph inside the pilot subsystem.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/pilot.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/replay.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_pilot.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_pilot_context.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/golden_helpers.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_weird_conventions.py` (remove the allowlist entries as debt is retired)",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pilot",
    "python",
    "refactor",
  ],
